acceptance_criteria: Release workflow verifies exact tag/package equality; Existing-tag recovery runs all non-pretag release gates; npm publication remains idempotent
definition_of_ready: The failed tag-triggered run proves exact tag/package equality passed and only the pre-tag next-version assertion failed.
parent: searx-repo-health-2026
reviewer: repository-owner
risk: high
confidence: 100
sprint: 2026-07-release-automation
release: next
reporter: codex-release-agent
severity: high
environment: Tag-triggered and manual recovery Release workflow
repro_steps: "Run Release for an existing tag whose package version matches the tag; release:dry-run rejects it as the next version."
resolution: Tagged publication now validates the immutable tag/package pair and runs every remaining release gate without incorrectly predicting a subsequent version.
expected_result: Existing-tag recovery and future tag pushes can reach idempotent npm publication.
actual_result: All tag-context gates pass locally against v2026.7.21; manual workflow recovery will verify the protected environment after merge.
affected_version: v2026.7.21 release workflow
component: release
regression: true
customer_impact: The tagged package cannot publish until recovery validation uses tag semantics.
